High-level summary for management:

Following CyberArk account discovery, newly found service accounts are temporarily placed in a single staging safe because the discovery process cannot automatically assign them to the correct team based on our internal application-ownership codes. To close this gap, we are introducing an automated process that reads each account's application code from Active Directory, matches it to the owning team's existing CyberArk safe, and relocates the account into the correct safe. Once moved, the process automatically triggers a credential reconciliation so each account is brought under full CyberArk management with a secured, rotated password — ensuring every service account ends up under the right team's ownership with no manual sorting and no disruption to the applications that rely on them.
